        "descriptions": [
          {
            "description": "The hybrid has occurred spontaneously in a privat garden between plants of the Azorean Leontodon hochstetteri planted in the first decade of the 20th century in Seefeld, Tirol, and the common L. hispidus subsp. hispidus. Since at least 2014 no individuals of the original L. hochstetteri but only of the hybrid have survived. The case indicates that L. hochstetteri and perhaps also the other Azorean Leontodon endemics would be highly endangered by introduced L. hispidus plants, because apparently no genetic barrier exists between these species."
          },
          {
            "description": "Morphologically intermediate between the parents. Leaf size and shape resemble L. hochstetteri but the lamina is narrower and of softer texture, and the leaves are more distinctly petiolate than in that speceis. Size and colour of the flowering capitula resemble L. hispidus. Flowering stems are branched ones, producing two capitula. The anchor hairs on the leaves are bi-to trifid."
          }
